@comment{
  AILM bibliography. Read by Pandoc with --natbib during PDF rendering.

  Policy for this file: every entry is a work whose existence, authorship, venue,
  and year the author can state without guessing. Fields that could not be
  confirmed are OMITTED rather than filled with a plausible value — a fabricated
  page range or DOI is worse than a missing one, because it is not visibly
  missing.

  A `note` field RENDERS into the printed reference list, so it is reserved for
  what a reader of the bibliography needs: an edition, a locator, what a resource
  is. Provenance uncertainty about this file is not that, and it lives here
  instead, because a bibliography comment block never renders. Entry by entry:

  brier1950 — the registered DOI is of the form 10.1175/1520-0493(1950)078<0001:
  VOFEIT>2.0.CO;2. The angle brackets do not survive a LaTeX text-mode round
  trip, so the field is omitted rather than mangled.

  obuchowski1998clustered — same angle-bracket DOI form, same treatment. The DOI
  is 10.1002/(SICI)1097-0258(19980715)17:13<1495::AID-SIM863>3.0.CO;2-I.

  coecke2010mathematical — Linguistic Analysis 36, the Lambek Festschrift issue.
  Several secondary bibliographies give the pages as 345--384, but neither DBLP
  nor Crossref indexes the journal version at all; both hold only the arXiv
  preprint. The range stays omitted until the printed issue is checked.

  chen1999empirical — the Crossref deposit for the registered DOI records the
  range as 359--393 while the range in circulation is 359--394; the publisher's
  own landing page was not reachable at audit time, so the conflict is left
  unresolved and the commonly printed 359--394 is kept rather than picking the
  registrar's figure without confirmation.

  Unresolved-field register, from the 2026-09-08 primary-source audit (84 of 97
  entries fully field-verified against a reachable primary record, after the N1
  pass below). Two classes. CONFIRMED METADATA CONFLICT (one): chen1999empirical
  above. SOURCE UNAVAILABLE (no reachable primary record confirms the named
  field; the entry keeps or omits it rather than guessing): brown1992entropy,
  marcus1993penn, holm1979 — no digital primary record for these journal years
  is reachable; fillmore1968case, lamb1966outline, lockwood1972introduction,
  makkai1973readings, francis1979brown, miller1955note — pre-digital books and
  chapters with no online publisher or registration record (the extent
  disagreements for lamb1966outline and lockwood1972introduction are noted
  above); parr2022active, bird2009nltk — the recorded ISBNs could not be checked
  against any reachable publisher or bookseller record; coecke2010mathematical —
  the journal identity per the note above. Three entries left this register
  during the same day's passes. jax2018: the official JAX CITATION.bib supplied
  the missing twelfth author (Katariya). smollm_2024: the release post's byline
  names exactly three authors, so the former `and others` was dropped. cmudict
  (N1): the note's unsupported `Version 0.7b` field was omitted under the
  omit-don't-guess policy once the pinned commit confirmed no reachable version
  designation; repository, title, URL, and the BSD-2-Clause license are verified
  against the upstream repository.

  vaswani2017attention, brown2020language, dwork2015adaptive — the NeurIPS
  proceedings site publishes no page numbers for these years. The ranges in
  circulation come from the Curran print volumes, which were not checked here.

  hoffmann2022training — also appears in the NeurIPS 2022 proceedings; those page
  numbers were not confirmed. Its author list, and those of brown2020language,
  liang2023holistic, is truncated with `and others`,
  which is a BibTeX convention rather than a defect.

  liang2023holistic — TMLR assigns neither volume nor article number.

  qwen25_2024 — the technical report credits the Qwen Team collectively and
  prints no individual author list.

  fillmore1968case — the paper circulated in 1967 as a pre-print for the Texas
  symposium of 13--15 April 1967 (ERIC ED019631) and was published in the 1968
  Bach & Harms volume. Both dates are correct for different objects; the entry
  is the published chapter, so it carries 1968. Citations giving 1967 for the
  chapter are conflating the pre-print with the publication.

  lamb1966prolegomena — Crossref records the issue as 42(2); the article is
  widely cited as 42(3). The volume and page range are secure and the issue
  number is not, so `number` is omitted rather than picking a side.

  lamb1966outline, lockwood1972introduction — total extents in circulation
  disagree (109 vs v+109; 305 vs 365). Neither is needed to cite a book, so
  neither is recorded.

  reich1968symbols — a Linguistic Automation Project report, not a journal
  article. Reprinted as chapter 6 of makkai1973readings. The `note` carries the
  ERIC accession because that is where a reader obtains the full text.

  fillmore1977reopened — Crossref confirms the series volume, pages, publisher
  and date but the editors were not verified, so `editor` is omitted.

  A note on what is NOT here. A. Kornai's survey reports, citing Borgida, that
  Lamb's 1966 formalism is essentially equivalent to finite automata. That is a
  claim this manuscript would like to make, and it is left uncited: the reading
  is two removes from a primary source and the survey's own venue and year were
  not confirmed. The finite-state position is attributed to reich1969finiteness
  instead, which argues it directly and is fully indexed.

  cmudict — the customary `0.7b` label carries no dated release on the upstream
  repository (and no reachable upstream file asserts the string; see the
  register), so the year is omitted.

  friedman2024cerebrum, friedman2024ccd — the keys say 2024 and both works are
  dated later; the years inside the entries are the correct ones. The keys are
  cited from several sections and were left alone rather than renamed piecemeal.
  The DOI previously recorded for friedman2024cerebrum, 10.5281/zenodo.12812427,
  resolves to an unrelated 2023 taxonomic record and has been replaced with the
  version DOI of the release the project actually reads. Zenodo identifies that
  record as v1.4 dated 2025-04-16, while the deposited PDF title page prints
  Version 1.2 (2025-04-12). Both identities are retained in the rendered note
  and in data/reference_sources.json.

  friedman2024ccd — the Zenodo record at 10.5281/zenodo.19695260 is titled
  "Compositional Approaches to Linguistic Case for Cognitive Modeling"; the title
  page of the exact deposited PDF prints "Cognitive Diagrams: Reviewing
  Categorical Accounts of Linguistic Case" and is dated 2026-04-22. The optional
  companion repository at the pinned revision declares that printed-title work
  as v2.3. The entry follows the archival record, because that is what a reader
  resolving the DOI is shown, while the note preserves the deposited identity.

  marneffe2021universal — added 2026-09-28 during the multi-lane bibliography
  merge. The Crossref deposit for 10.1162/coli_a_00402 carries no volume or
  issue and gives page "1-54" (an early/typeset-stage registration). The ACL
  Anthology record for the same DOI (2021.cl-2.11, MIT Press, Cambridge, MA)
  gives the print pagination actually used by the venue: Computational
  Linguistics 47(2):255-308. The entry follows the ACL Anthology print
  pagination rather than the incomplete Crossref deposit, consistent with the
  chen1999empirical precedent above of preferring the circulating publisher
  record over a conflicting registrar figure.

  smekal2023gnn, pezzulo2024generating, wong2023word, schick2023toolformer,
  yao2023react — added 2026-09-29 during the future-directions/related-work
  bibliography merge. Four independent lanes proposed overlapping subsets of
  these five keys for the new Future Directions discussion and the expanded
  Related Work survey; each was re-verified here directly against its primary
  record before merge (Zenodo record 7803328 for smekal2023gnn; Crossref DOI
  10.1016/j.tics.2023.10.002 for pezzulo2024generating; the arXiv Atom API for
  2302.04761, 2210.03629, and 2306.12672) rather than trusting either lane's
  report. All fields agree across the lanes' proposals and this
  re-verification, so no conflict needed resolving. yao2023react carries the
  ICLR 2023 publication year, matching this file's existing convention for
  arXiv preprints later published in ICLR proceedings (see e.g.
  sclar2024quantifying below, an ICLR paper cited by its eprint); the paper's
  first arXiv submission was 2022-10-06.
}

